      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by quantum dot-labeled anti-HA antibody detection in cortical neurons; single particle tracking of surface stargazin trajectories performed. Explicit functional assay (e.g., AMPA receptor currents) NOT MEASURED in the cited clips.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "L3 explicitly states 'this tag is extracellular when stargazin is in the plasma membrane', confirming the HA tag is surface-exposed on the full-length membrane-anchored protein. CACNG2 has two extracellular regions: ECL1 (31-105, 75 aa) and ECL2 (158-177, 20 aa); neither is named in the ledger. ECL1 is assigned as the region because it is the large extracellular loop and the canonical location for HA insertion in stargazin constructs (the Bats et al. 2007 method referenced in L4). No residue is named in any ledger clip, so insert_after_residue is null. HA-tagged stargazin (CACNG2/TARP gamma-2) expressed as full-length membrane-anchored protein in cortical neurons; the HA epitope is confirmed extracellular by quantum dot-labeled secondary antibody detection and single particle tracking experiments. The construct is used as a tool for surface diffusion tracking. No specific residue or loop is named in the ledger; ECL1 (residues 31-105) is the large extracellular loop of this 4-TM protein and the canonical location for HA in published stargazin constructs.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 30271322,
          "citation": "PMID 30271322",
          "claim": "To track in real time the movement of stargazin at the cell surface we transfected cortical neurons with constructs encoding Homer1C-GFP, for postsynaptic labeling, and HA-tagged stargazin; this tag is extracellular when stargazin is in the plasma membrane (Figure 2A )."
