  "literature_notes": "L1-L5 all confirm an extracellular HA tag on CACNG2/stargazin in full-length, membrane-anchored constructs expressed in cortical neurons, but none name a specific residue or loop. CACNG2 has two extracellular loops: ECL1 (31-105) and ECL2 (158-177); ECL1 is assigned as the region because it is the large extracellular loop and the canonical location for HA in stargazin constructs (Bats et al. 2007, referenced in L4), but this is an inference not directly stated in the ledger. L6 (GFP-tagged TARP gamma-2) describes a biochemical purification construct used for FSEC analysis; the GFP position is not stated and the tag is not confirmed to be extracellular. For a 4-TM protein with intracellular N- and C-termini (residues 1-9 and 199-323 respectively), GFP is most likely C-terminal (intracellular) for biochemical detection purposes. L6 does not qualify as a surface tag site and is excluded. The N-terminus (1-9) and C-terminus (199-323) of CACNG2 are both intracellular and do not qualify as extracellular tag sites.",
